% podman-config-ls 1

## NAME
podman\-config\-ls - List all available configs (alias list)

## SYNOPSIS
**podman config ls** [*options*]

## DESCRIPTION

Lists all the configs that exist. The output can be formatted to a Go template using the **--format** option.

## OPTIONS

@@option filter.config-ls

#### **--format**=*format*

Format config output using Go template.

Valid placeholders for the Go template are listed below:

| **Placeholder**          | **Description**                                                   |
| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| .CreatedAt               | When config was created (relative timestamp, human-readable)      |
| .Driver                  | Driver name (string)                                              |
| .ID                      | ID of config                                                      |
| .Name                    | Name of config                                                    |
| .UpdatedAt               | When config was last updated (relative timestamp, human-readable) |

@@option noheading

#### **--quiet**, **-q**

Print config IDs only.

## EXAMPLES

List all configs.
```
$ podman config ls
```

List the name field of all configs.
```
$ podman config ls --format "{{.Name}}"
```

List all configs whose name includes the specified string.
```
$ podman config ls --filter name=confidential
```

